## Known LLM-as-a-Judge Biases and How to Mitigate Them
### Self-Preference Bias (Self-Enhancement)
Models tend to rate their own outputs, or outputs from the same model family, higher than outputs from other models. This self-enhancement effect has been documented across several model families and is thought to be related to [perplexity](https://www.comet.com/site/blog/perplexity-for-llm-evaluation/): models find text that matches their own training distribution more “natural” and therefore score it higher.

